  "title": "About Hear Plugin",
  "story": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "ba9751a5511afdbf",
      "text": "The **Hear** plugin walks a page-level GMap as a street and lets its pages speak: positional audio under a versioned soundscape policy, a deadband and an equal-power crossfade so voices do not flicker, a consent gate before anything sounds, and a transcript and provenance card for every voice. Built by Phase 3 of the Hear Crowds Plan on atlas.anarchive.earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "hear",
      "id": "36944e2bc3d2768e",
      "text": "MAP https://atlas.anarchive.earth/assets/hear-crowds-demo/map.json\nMEDIA https://atlas.anarchive.earth/assets/hear-crowds-demo/street-media.json\nPOLICY https://atlas.anarchive.earth/assets/hear-crowds-demo/soundscape-policy.json\nSTREET clause.legalcommons.org/right-to-amparo\nHEIGHT 520\nRight to Amparo and its sixteen houses, speaking."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "a7e1b8e9d6e34ef6",
      "text": "# Commands\n\nOne per line, UPPERCASE first word. Anything else is the caption."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "cd4c1040c3c51e52",
      "text": "- `MAP url` \u2014 the map.json a page-level GMap writes: positions, regions, edges, the street\n- `MEDIA url` \u2014 the street-media.json index: which houses speak and where their clips and manifests are\n- `POLICY url` \u2014 the soundscape-policy.json: emitter budget, intelligible limit, ducking, crossfade, deadband, dwell, weights\n- `STREET site/slug` \u2014 the square; defaults to the map's own street\n- `HEIGHT px` \u2014 the height of the place, 240 or more\n- `FLIGHT url` (or `FLIGHT auto`) \u2014 an authored flight that owns the camera and the mix: circle the city, dive to a house and land inside its first sentence, cross to a neighbour that speaks another language, climb, circle again. The Take the flight button, on the gate and on the bar."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "73838ab426fb0a98",
      "text": "# How it sounds\n\nNothing plays before Enter the soundscape. Then a listener rides the camera and only the policy's budget of houses emit, ranked by proximity, focus and view direction. A house outside the intelligible limit murmurs through a low-pass filter. A challenger must beat the weakest voice by the deadband, and that voice must have dwelt at least the minimum before it gives way; every change is an equal-power crossfade. Click a house, or pick one from Solo, to stand at its threshold: the house starts its clause from the top the moment you arrive, the transcript follows from its first line, and it stops looping while you listen so the end of the clause is an event. Walk carries you round the street by way of the square, house to house, each clause from the top on arrival and a beat after it ends; Next skips on; any walking key hands the place back to you. Close returns everything to the beginning: silent, above the square, the gate up. Read along at the threshold; go inside for the page, its audio and its provenance; open the source page in the wiki from either. Without WebGL the street is a list of houses with players.\n\n# Controls\n\nDrag to look; W A S D walk, Q E up and down, or hold the arrow pad; F or the Full screen button fills the display, Esc leaves; Mute silences every bus, Pause voices stops the clips and keeps the place; Listening trial runs the One Audible Street questions."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "id": "927870f092672760",
      "text": "# The flight and the stage (0.9.0)\n\n**Take the flight** runs a cue sheet of stages: `orbit`, `dive`, `listen`, `glide`, `listen`, `climb`, and round again. The camera rides one smooth curve per stage, its speed matched where one stage hands over to the next. The flight sets the mix itself: from above, one voice per sector of the city murmurs in its own language; on the way down that bed fades with altitude; a few seconds before arrival the house starts its clause from the top and is the only clear voice; its neighbours murmur softly. A caption card names the house, its language and its voice, and shows the words as they are spoken. Any walking key, a drag or the wheel hands the controls back.\n\n**Full screen holds.** Full screen lifts the place out of the wiki's lineup into a window-sized layer before asking the browser for full screen, so nothing the wiki does to the item can drop it. Leaving the browser's full screen keeps the window-sized layer; Esc again, the button or Close put the place back on the page. A trackpad or wheel moves you over the ground and never scrolls or swipes the page underneath.\n\n**Names stay out of the way.** By default only the square and the houses speaking clearly carry a name, small, hidden behind buildings and faded with distance. Names (or L) cycles speaking, all near, off.\n\n**Nothing clips.** Every bus runs through a master that makes room as voices pile up and a limiter before the listener. The murmur is a soft low-pass rather than a 700 Hz wall."
    },
    {
